# NOTICE

jevmlx is an unofficial, open-source Jev-style engine for Apple Silicon. It
builds on two prior works:

- [rorshopping/jev-on-a-laptop](https://github.com/rorshopping/jev-on-a-laptop)
  (MIT) — the research repository this project started from: benchmarks,
  evaluation methodology, and documentation of the parallel constrained
  decoding technique on Apple Silicon.
- [harshatheg/Qwen-2.5-1B-RLCD](https://huggingface.co/harshatheg/Qwen-2.5-1B-RLCD)
  (Apache-2.0) — an MLX demo of parallel constrained decoding with one 1.5B
  checkpoint; the original engine whose approach jevmlx reimplements. jevmlx
  is the maintained, generic version: any MLX instruct model or
  OpenAI-compatible server, choices in the prompt, multi-select, UNKNOWN,
  per-field probability, an eval harness.

Jev is a product of TypeSafe AI. jevmlx is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or connected to TypeSafe AI.
